266 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 151 0 R
/E (Education in rural India faces a multitude of challenges: inadequate infrastructure, shortage of trained teachers, high dropout rates, and limited access to digital learning resources. These issues not only widen the urban-rural divide but also impact the future employability and empowerment of rural youth. Persistent socio-economic disparities have further heightened the urgency for inclusive and accessible educational solutions.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [13]
>>
endobj
267 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 151 0 R
/E <>
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [14]
>>
endobj
268 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 151 0 R
/E (In this edition, our Sector News segment explores rural education in depth, featuring an insightful interview with industry experts. Campus News highlights a range of activities, including guest talks, sessions by industry partners, and other vibrant events. We also bring you cherished reminiscences from our alumni about their personal and professional journeys at KSRM. Adding a creative touch, students have contributed their photography, paintings, and thoughtful articles, enriching this edition further.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [15]
>>
endobj
269 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 151 0 R
/E (The Newsletter Committee extends heartfelt thanks to Prof. Nirmal K. Mandal, Prof. Somnath Dutta, and Prof. Surendra Jena for their invaluable guidance in giving this edition a global perspective. We are equally grateful to our Director Prof. Sarbeswar Mohanty, Dean Prof. Sukumar Dash, our faculty members, support staff, seniors, and academic peers for their unwavering encouragement. Without their collective support, this edition would not have been possible.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [16]
>>
endobj
