/S /H3
/P 163 0 R
/T (4.If you could introduce one transformative policy or systemic reform to strengthen India's rural education system, what would it be, and why do you believe it would have the greatest long-term impact?)
/E (4.If you could introduce one transformative policy or systemic reform to strengthen India's rural education system, what would it be, and why do you believe it would have the greatest long-term impact?)
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
383 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H4
/P 163 0 R
/T (Introducing a comprehensive Rural Education Empowerment Strategy that integrates digital infrastructure, teacher training, and community participation would be transformative. This policy would ensure equitable access to quality education through widespread internet connectivity, enabling remote learning and digital resources. Simultaneously, it would focus on training teachers to adapt to digital and inclusive pedagogies, fostering student engagement. Incorporating local community involvement would promote ownership and sustainability of educational initiatives.)
/E (Introducing a comprehensive Rural Education Empowerment Strategy that integrates digital infrastructure, teacher training, and community participation would be transformative. This policy would ensure equitable access to quality education through widespread internet connectivity, enabling remote learning and digital resources. Simultaneously, it would focus on training teachers to adapt to digital and inclusive pedagogies, fostering student engagement. Incorporating local community involvement would promote ownership and sustainability of educational initiatives.)
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
