441 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 169 0 R
/E (Some of the most meaningful lessons are learned beyond classrooms. My internship with RAF Global under the Alkem Anaemia Mukht Abhiyan \(AAMA\), supported by the Alkem Foundation, offered me an opportunity to explore the human side of public health. Travelling through communities in Jaisalmer, Barmer, and Balotra, I witnessed how conversations, trust, and consistent engagement can influence healthier choices. )
/Pg 30 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
442 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 169 0 R
/E (Through household surveys, Focus Group Discussions, Key Informant Interviews, and field observations, I assessed the impact of Behaviour Change Interventions while interacting with beneficiaries and frontline health workers. Every interaction revealed that sustainable change begins with understanding people's realities before designing solutions. This experience strengthened my skills in impact assessment and Monitoring & Evaluation while shaping a deeper appreciation for community-driven development. It reaffirmed my belief that true impact is not just reflected in data, but in the confidence, resilience, and aspirations of the communities we serve.)
/Pg 30 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
