/E (As part of my MTS-I internship with BAIF Institute for Sustainable Livelihoods and Development \(BISLD\), under the MBA in Rural Management program at KIIT School of Rural Management, I gained hands-on exposure to rural livelihood interventions under the Mor Jal Mor Maati project across Korba district, Chhattisgarh.)
/Pg 31 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
454 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 170 0 R
/E (The internship allowed me to lead an impact assessment of Solar Insect Traps \(SIT\) and Water Lifting Devices, surveying farmers across four project clusters to evaluate adoption, satisfaction, and economic benefits. I also contributed to the promotion of Farmer Producer Organisations \(FPOs\), which gave me direct interaction with community members and helped me understand interventions both from the farmers' lived experience and the organisation's implementation lens. Field visits, structured surveys, and stakeholder dialogues across agriculture, livestock, water resources, and NTFP promotion strengthened my skills in data collection, impact analysis, and grassroots-level engagement, reinforcing my interest in evidence-based rural development.)
/Pg 31 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
