465 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 171 0 R
/E (During our internship at the United Nations World Food Programme \(UN-WFP\) India Country Office, we had the opportunity to serve as UN Volunteer Programme Support Assistants, contributing to two flagship initiatives - ENACT in Assam and RIISE in Odisha. Our work centred on exploring Climate Adaptation Planning \(CAP\), climate vulnerability assessments, programme documentation, and knowledge management, providing valuable insights into how evidence-based planning strengthens climate-resilient rural development.)
/Pg 32 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
466 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 171 0 R
/E (The highlight of our internship was a field exposure in Assam, where we observed climate-smart interventions such as Integrated Farming Systems, Nutri Gardens, Smart Seed Production Systems, Climate Adaptation Information Centres, and other Nature-Based Solutions, bringing our desk-based learning to life. Interactions with communities, implementing partners, and WFP professionals deepened our understanding of participatory planning, institutional convergence, local ownership, and sustainable livelihoods.)
/Pg 32 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
467 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 171 0 R
/E (More than an internship, it was a journey of learning, collaboration, and discovery that strengthened our analytical, documentation, communication, and programme management skills. The experience broadened our perspective on sustainable rural development and reinforced our belief that meaningful and lasting change is achieved when communities, institutions, and innovation work together to build a climate-resilient future.)
/Pg 32 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
