490 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 173 0 R
/E (As part of the MBA \(Rural Management\) programme at KIIT School of Rural Management \(KSRM\), I completed a two-month Management Traineeship \(MTS-1\) with Transform Rural India Foundation \(TRIF\) in Petlawad Block, Jhabua, Madhya Pradesh. My study, "Practices and Behaviour Shift After Community Health Interventions," assessed the impact of community-based health, nutrition, and WASH initiatives across six tribal villages. Using household surveys, Focus Group Discussions, and Key Informant Interviews, )
/Pg 34 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
491 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 173 0 R
/E (I engaged with adolescent girls, pregnant women, SHG members, and frontline health workers. The findings highlighted positive behavioural changes, including increased awareness of menstrual hygiene, improved Iron and Folic Acid \(IFA\) consumption, higher Antenatal Care \(ANC\) visits, better maternal healthcare practices, and active SHG participation in promoting nutrition and sanitation. The internship strengthened my research, communication, and field engagement skills while demonstrating how community participation and grassroots institutions can drive sustainable improvements in rural health and well-being.)
/Pg 34 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
