2145 0 obj
<<
/Title <352E496620796F752068616420746865206F70706F7274756E69747920746F206368616E6765206A757374206F6E6520617370656374206F6620496E646961907320727572616C20656475636174696F6E2073797374656D20746F6461792C207768617420776F756C6420697420626520616E64207768793F>
/Dest [28 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 2138 0 R
/First 2152 0 R
/Last 2152 0 R
/Count -1
>>
endobj
2146 0 obj
<<
/Title (Governments should introduce robust policy frameworks, allocate funds for human resources, textbooks, TLM, and infrastructure, ensuring equitable access to quality education.Educational institutions must innovate curricula, train teachers, and promote inclusive practices.)
/Dest [24 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 2141 0 R
/Next 2147 0 R
>>
endobj
2147 0 obj
<<
/Title (NGOs can provide grassroots support, and foster community engagement, encouraging local ownership. CSR initiatives from corporations can supplement funding, infrastructure, and technological access, bridging resource gaps. Local communities are vital for ensuring cultural relevance, participation, and sustainability.)
/Dest [24 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 2141 0 R
/Prev 2146 0 R
>>
endobj
2148 0 obj
<<
/Title (Introducing a comprehensive Rural Education Empowerment Strategy that integrates digital infrastructure, teacher training, and community participation would be transformative. This policy would ensure equitable access to quality education through widespread internet connectivity, enabling remote learning and digital resources. Simultaneously, it would focus on training teachers to adapt to digital and inclusive pedagogies, fostering student engagement. Incorporating local community involvement would promote ownership and sustainability of educational initiatives.)
/Dest [24 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 2142 0 R
>>
endobj
2149 0 obj
<<
/Title (5.With the rapid growth of AI, digital learning, and educational technology, how can these innovations be leveraged to improve learning outcomes in rural areas while addressing challenges such as digital access, infrastructure, and teacher preparedness?)
/Dest [25 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 2143 0 R
>>
endobj
2150 0 obj
<<
/Title (1.What, in your opinion, are the challenges preventing rural India from achieving quality education for all?)
/Dest [26 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 2144 0 R
/Next 2153 0 R
>>
endobj
2151 0 obj
<<
/Title (3.How can governments, educational institutions, NGOs, CSR initiatives and local communities collaborate more effectively to transform rural education?)
/Dest [27 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 2144 0 R
/Prev 2153 0 R
>>
endobj
2152 0 obj
<<
/Title (If I could change one aspect, I would strengthen the teacher ecosystem, beginning with ensuring that teachers posted in rural schools have access to government accommodation within or near the villages they serve. When teachers become part of the community rather than daily commuters, they develop a stronger sense of ownership towards the school and its students. It also encourages regular interaction with parents, builds trust within the community and improves accountability, creating a more supportive learning environment. At the same time, educational planning must be driven by accurate and regularly updated UDISE data. Reliable data enables timely teacher deployment, identifies infrastructure gaps and supports evidence-based decision-making. Together, empowered teachers and informed planning can significantly improve the quality of rural education.)
/Dest [28 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 2145 0 R
>>
endobj
2153 0 obj
<<
/Title (2.Based on your experience, which intervention or innovation has had the most significant impact on improving rural education, and what made it successful?)
/Dest [26 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 2144 0 R
/Prev 2150 0 R
/Next 2151 0 R
>>
endobj
